column1651:
24/May/26 6:07 PM;5f3432cde115420046434665;[~accountid:712020:f9a894b1-f824-4a33-a40d-1d507fe78d86] No, QA was set up to send to SIT. I assumed this was not correct and changed it to send to Enovia QA. I have now set this back to SIT.  

If Enovia SIT is not receiving updates, we will likely need to do a live troubleshooting session, as we are receiving messages back from Enovia SIT suggesting that the update was, in fact, received:

{noformat}Response: rawResponse is {"Icons": [     {         "iconId": "1637",         "iconGS1": "Icon With Variable Text Master Graphic",         "iconGENo": "MAE-00030061",         "iconRev": "C",         "iconCanonicalId": "1637",         "comment": "",        {noformat}

column1653:
30/May/26 4:27 PM;5f3432cde115420046434665;[~accountid:712020:f9a894b1-f824-4a33-a40d-1d507fe78d86] The reason that these Icons did not flow into Enovia and did not receive a MAE number is because the Icons were created with trailing spaces in the Names during import.  This resulted in dynamically generated filenames and embedded spaces in the filenames within JSON – almost certainly the culprit for this response from Enovia…

{{{"Icons": [{     "iconId": "1091",     "iconGS1": "",     "iconGENo": "",     "iconRev": "",     "iconCanonicalId": "1091",     "comment": "Icon File is Empty.",     "iconFileName": "",     "status": "Failed" }]}}}

We have [scoured the code|https://github.com/procter-gamble/canvas/pull/1729] for spots in which we can Trim the strings provided in Excel to prevent this in the future. But at its heart, this was a classic “Garbage In Garbage Out” issue.

